# FIXED in forge-lang 8d1bb528 (all four corners now trim alike). Repro (forge-lang a4149718): a 4-flange box, all flanges up and inside, auto corner trim. Three
# corners trim alike; the corner between `right` (outline[1]) and `rear` (outline[2]) does not. In the
# flat, at (+x, +y), the rear flange stops 3.42 shorter (93.56 vs 96.98 from the centre) and the right
# flange runs 3.42 longer (71.98 vs 68.56). The relief arc there is also placed differently. Expected:
# all four corners alike (the part is symmetric).
# Run: fg run box_corner.fg --dxf box.dxf, then compare the CUT line ends near each corner.
shared t = 3.02
shared W = 200
shared D = 150
shared H = 30
sketch plan(on: offset(xy, t)) {
  outline = rect(center: (0, 0), size: (W, D))
}
floor = sheet(plan, t: t, r: 1.6, bend: kfactor(ratio(0.38)))
front = flange(floor.edge(plan.outline[0]), height: H)
right = flange(floor.edge(plan.outline[1]), height: H)
rear = flange(floor.edge(plan.outline[2]), height: H)
left = flange(floor.edge(plan.outline[3]), height: H)
flat = unfold(floor)
